	(text_box "## Hardware MCP servers (all work in Claude Code, Codex and agy)\n\n**1. kicad**: reviews your KiCad project\n- Runs ERC and DRC, checks that footprints match the schematic, runs a manufacturing (DFM) check and builds a BOM with prices.\n- It's set to read-only, so it reviews files but doesn't edit them.\n\n**2. atopile**: lets you design circuits as code\n- Finds and installs packages, adds JLCPCB parts and builds the project.\n\n**3. pcbparts**: the main tool for finding parts (fastest, no login)\n- `jlc_search` searches with filters like voltage, current and package. It also gives datasheets, pinouts, alternatives and live stock.\n- Can look up parts on Mouser and DigiKey, recommend sensors and show reference boards.\n- `cse_get_kicad` downloads ready-made KiCad symbols and footprints.\n\n**4. jlc**: turns JLC/EasyEDA parts into KiCad library parts\n- `library_install` adds a part by its LCSC number, and `library_batch_install` adds several at once.\n\n**5. jlcpcb-catalog**: local copy of the JLCPCB catalog with live stock and prices\n- Searches parts, checks stock and prices, gets datasheets and estimates PCB costs.\n- ⚠️ It also has tools that place real JLCPCB orders. Don't use those without checking first.\n\n**Typical workflow:** find parts with pcbparts → check stock and prices with jlcpcb-catalog → add them to your KiCad library with jlc → check the design with kicad."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 301.625 26.035 0)
		(size 71.755 70.485)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
